WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.470
BTS is everywhere,

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.058
and people can't get enough of them.

00:00:10.058 --> 00:00:10.891
- BTS!

00:00:13.051 --> 00:00:14.153
- Please welcome, BTS!

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.420
After finding success in South Korea,

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.570
they were able to make a
huge splash internationally.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.110
Tickets for their global
concert tour sold out

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:26.140
within hours of being released.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.110
They became the first-ever K-pop act

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:32.163
to make a No. 1 album with
2018's "Love Yourself: Tear."

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.560
And they're not stopping anytime soon.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.880
Their newest album "Map
of the Soul: Persona"

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.410
is already looking like
it'll be a huge hit,

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.850
and of course, people
camped outside for days

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.950
to see them perform live
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:50.040
But BTS wasn't an overnight sensation.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.540
It took them years of hard
work to get to this level.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.240
BTS debuted in June 2013,
and they quickly gained

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.130
a dedicated fan base
thanks to social media.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.930
They show a lot of love and
appreciation for their fans

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:04.520
who they even named A.R.M.Y.,

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.520
which means Adorable
Representatives for MC Youth.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:12.190
And in 2017, BTS won the Top
Social Artist Billboard Award,

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:15.040
breaking Justin Bieber's
six-year winning streak

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.930
and making them the first K-pop act

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.920
to win a Billboard Music Award.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.884
Unsurprisingly, they won again in 2018.

00:01:21.884 --> 00:01:22.717
- BTS!

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.660
- [Narrator] BTS also
became the first K-pop band

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:32.630
to perform at the American
Music Awards in 2017,

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:35.230
gaining them even more
fans internationally.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:36.680
But their fans don't just love them

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:38.830
for their mind-blowing performances.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:42.080
They love BTS for their
socially conscious music.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.880
BTS writes their own music,
which tackles complex topics

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.233
like bullying, mental health,
and societal pressures.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.750
BTS stands for Bangtan Sonyeondan,

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.510
or Bulletproof Boy Scouts in English.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.160
According to member J-Hope,

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.990
the name signifies the group's desire

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:03.490
to block out stereotypes,
criticisms, and expectations

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.620
that are imposed on adolescents.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:07.270
Essentially, they're bulletproof.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:09.920
Their work is also inspired

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.370
by literature, art, and even philosophy.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:16.080
Their music video for "Blood,
Sweat, and Tears" references

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.070
and showcases a few
famous European paintings,

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.250
and their newest album is based

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.210
off the book "Jung's Map of the Soul,"

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:25.530
which explores the theories of
Swiss psychiatrist Carl Jung.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.150
Mostly, fans can't get enough

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.410
of the chemistry among the members.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:31.580
The band consists of seven members:

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:32.413
RM,

00:02:32.413 --> 00:02:33.780
Jin,

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:34.840
Suga,

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.010
J-Hope,

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.160
Jimin,

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.050
V,

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:38.883
and Jungkook.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.250
Since becoming a global sensation,

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.860
they've collaborated
with many famous artists

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.000
including American DJ Steve Aoki

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.466
who remixed "Mic Drop"

00:02:48.466 --> 00:02:51.083
and collaborated on "The Truth Untold."

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:52.850
On the heels of the remixes,

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:57.310
Aoki featured BTS members
Jungkook and RM in "Wasted on Me."

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.370
This is the members' first
all-English-language song.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.470
BTS also released an alternative version

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:05.490
of their song "Idol"
featuring Nicki Minaj.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:08.220
The music video received
over 45 million views

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.470
in its first 24 hours on YouTube,

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.300
breaking the then-record previously set

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.853
by Taylor Swift with "Look
What You Made Me Do."

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.840
Their newest album features
even more collaborations,

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.520
this time with Ed Sheeran on
a track called "Make it Right"

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.570
and Halsey on "Boy with Love."

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.480
This collaboration is already
blowing up on YouTube.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.780
With yet another hit on their hands,

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.317
the sky's the limit for BTS.

